:TypeProvided a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    dcterms:description "For RecordType 141 – list P1.2; for 142 – list R14.2;For RecordType 143 – list W1.2;For RecordType 144 – list V2.2;For RecordType 151 – list W2.2;For RecordType 152 – list V3.4;For RecordType 161 – list P2.2;For RecordType 200 – list 4.14;For RecordType 210 – list V8.2;For RecordType 300 – list C2.2" ;
    rdfs:domain :ServiceFAReferral ;
    rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
    :linkedVocabulary :list_BedNight, :list_HOPWAFinancialAssistance, :list_HOPWAServices, :list_MovingOnAssistance, :list_PATHReferral, :list_PATHServices, :list_RHYServices, :list_SSVFFinancialAssistance, :list_SSVFServices, :list_VoucherTracking ;
    :responseValue """V3.4: 1=Rental assistance;10=Child care;2=Security deposit;3=Utility deposit;4=Utility fee payment assistance;5=Moving costs;8=Transportation services: tokens/vouchers;9=Transportation services: vehicle repair/maintenance;12=General housing stability assistance;14=Emergency housing assistance;15=Shallow Subsidy –Financial Assistance;16=Food assistance;17=Landlord Incentive;18=Tenant Incentive.

P1.2: 1=Re-engagement;10=Housing eligibility determination;11=Security deposits;
12=One-time rent for eviction prevention;14=Clinical assessment;2=Screening;
3=Habilitation/rehabilitation;4=Community mental health;5=Substance use treatment;
6=Case management;7=Residential supportive services;8=Housing minor renovation; 9=Housing moving assistance.

4.1.4: 200=BedNight

P2.2: 1=Community mental health;10=Medical insurance;11=Temporary housing;
2=Substance use treatment;3=Primary health/dental care;4=Job training;
5=Educational services;6=Housing services;7=Permanent housing;8=Income assistance;9=Employment assistance.

W1.2: 1=Adult day care and personal assistance;2=Case management;
3=Child care;4=Criminal justice/legal services;10=Mental health care/counseling;
11=Outreach and/or engagement;12=Substance use services/treatment;
13=Transportation;14=Other HOPWA funded service;5=Education;
6=Employment and training services;7=Food/meals/nutritional services;8=Health/medical care;9=Life skills training.

R14.2: 10=Parenting education for youth with children;12=Post-natal care for client (person who gave birth);13=Pre-natal care;14=Health/medical care;2=Community service/service learning (CSL);5=Education;6=Employment and/or training services;
7=Criminal justice /legal services;8=Life skills training;17=Substance use disorder treatment;18=Substance use disorder Ed/Prevention Services;26=Home-based Services;27=Post-natal newborn care (wellness exams; immunizations);28=STD Testing;29=Street-based Services.

V2.2: 1=Outreach services;2=Case management services;3=Assistance obtaining VA benefits;4=Assistance obtaining/coordinating other public benefits;5=Direct provision of other public benefits;6=Other (non-TFA) supportive service approved by VA;7=Shallow Subsidy;8=Returning Home;9=Rapid Resolution;10=Healthcare navigation.

V8.2: 1=Referral package forwarded to PHA;10=Veteran exited – family maintained the voucher;11=Veteran exited – prior to ever receiving a voucher;12=Other;2=Voucher denied by PHA;3=Voucher issued by PHA;4=Voucher revoked or expired;5=Voucher in use – veteran moved into housing;6=Voucher was ported locally;7=Voucher was administratively absorbed by new PHA;8=Voucher was converted to Housing Choice Voucher;9=Veteran exited – voucher was returned.

C2.2: 1=Subsidized housing application assistance;2=Financial assistance for Moving On;3=Non-financial assistance for Moving On;4=Housing referral/placement; 5=Other (please specify).

W2.2: 1=Rental assistance;2=Security deposits;3=Utility deposits;4=Utility payments; 7=Mortgage assistance.""" ;
    :responseValueSecondary "" .

